  "summary": "This study used LiF/HCl-etched, delaminated Ti3C2Tx flakes (average lateral size 219 \u00b1 47 nm) to prepare vacuum-filtered Ti3C2Tx\u2013SWCNT control papers and vertically aligned MXLLC films. The MXLLC films contained 10 wt% SWCNT spacers and were formed through C12E6-assisted lamellar liquid-crystal assembly, mechanical shear alignment, supercritical drying, and 550 \u00b0C annealing to remove surfactant. Eight distinct fabricated electrode specimens are identifiable from the reported architectures, thicknesses, and the pure-Ti3C2Tx control: two filtered Ti3C2Tx\u2013SWCNT papers, five MXLLC thicknesses, and one pure filtered Ti3C2Tx paper. The 200 \u00b5m MXLLC is the headline electrode, retaining over 200 F g\u22121 and an areal capacitance greater than 0.6 F cm\u22122 at 2,000 mV s\u22121 in 3 M H2SO4. BET area, porosity, pore size, final-film interlayer spacing, tortuosity, and most individual mass loadings were not reported."
